Operation of a compiler (handout order):
1. Pre-processing: text manipulation (macros, comments).
2. Lexical analysis: breaks the source code into tokens (identifiers, keywords).
3. Parsing: turns tokens into phrases (if-then, assignment, ...), building a syntax tree.
4. Semantic analysis: checks the meaning, e.g. variable types.
5. Code generation: produces machine-level code.
6. Optimisation: improves the code so it runs faster or uses fewer resources.
7. Linking: combines multiple code files / libraries into one executable.
